{"run_id": "20260802T125238-hepkg", "qid": "gen-union-f2f5cfe5", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many analyses estimate a background using Data-driven matrix method or Control-region-based normalization fit for $t\\bar{t}$+jets components?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql", "hops"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The graph records 44 analyses that estimate a background using either the Data-driven matrix method or the Control-region-based normalization fit for \\( t\\bar{t} \\)+jets components. \n\nThis count is based on the following methods found in the graph:\n- Data-driven normalization from control region fit (CR_ttbar), simultaneous with signal region\n- Control-region data-driven normalization\n- Data-driven matrix method\n- Control-region-based normalisation via simultaneous likelihood fit\n- Data-driven normalization from unconstrained fit parameter in signal region (global likelihood)\n- Control-region-based normalization fit for \\( t\\bar{t} \\)+jets components\n- Data-driven normalisation via simultaneous profile-likelihood fit in dedicated control regions\n- Control-region-based normalisation of \\( t\\bar{t} \\) background (profile likelihood fit, data/MC ratio in dedicated CR)\n- Control-region-based background normalisation via simultaneous profile likelihood fit\n- ABCD (matrix) data-driven background estimation using control regions in data with parametric fits\n- Data-driven multi-jet-enriched control-region template-fit method\n- Data-driven normalisation in kinematically similar control regions\n- MC-based prediction with free-floating normalization constrained via dedicated control region in combined fit\n- Free-floating normalization constrained by dedicated control regions in the fit\n- Normalization to data in dedicated control regions\n- WZ/ZZ control-region-constrained simultaneous fit\n- MC shape normalised via dedicated control-region fit\n- Data-driven eμ control-region method for top background\n- Data-driven fake-factor method\n- Normalisation floated in the combined fit without a dedicated control region\n- Likelihood-fit normalisation factors from control regions\n- Control-region fit to CRWZ2j data for \\( WZ \\)+jets normalisation\n- Background-only profile-likelihood fit normalization of mixed-data sample\n- Data-driven background estimation via smooth functional fit (BPDF) to \\( m_{Jγ} \\), validated with mass-sideband control samples\n- Data-driven tight-to-loose ratio method\n\nThese methods are used across 44 distinct papers.", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "Data-driven matrix method or Control-region-based normalization fit", "kind": "background_method"}, "rows": 60, "error": null, "seconds": 0.159}, {"round": 1, "tool": "count", "args": {"predicate": "background_uses_method", "object_set": "set_1"}, "rows": 1, "error": null, "seconds": 0.003}], "sets": {"set_1": ["hepkg:background_method:abcd_data_driven_crs", "hepkg:background_method:cr_normalisation_fit", "hepkg:background_method:data-control-sample-normalization", "hepkg:background_method:data_driven_fake_factor", "hepkg:background_method:discrete_profiling", "hepkg:method:abcd-method", "hepkg:method:abcd-reweighting", "hepkg:method:background_parametrization_fit_to_data", "hepkg:method:charge_misid_data_driven", "hepkg:method:control_region_data", "hepkg:method:control_region_normalization", "hepkg:method:control_region_normalization_fit", "hepkg:method:cr-constrained-fit-normalization", "hepkg:method:cr-data-driven-normalization", "hepkg:method:cr-normalisation-fit", "hepkg:method:cr-normalization", "hepkg:method:cr-normalization-fit", "hepkg:method:cr-normalization-ttbar", "hepkg:method:cr_fit_normalization", "hepkg:method:cr_transfer_factor", "hepkg:method:cross_section_normalization_variation", "hepkg:method:crw", "hepkg:method:crwz2j-fit", "hepk